    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Change a whole local video's playback speed and create a new video.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input media file path.\r\n          --output TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Output media file path.\r\n          --speed FLOAT:POSITIVE REQUIRED \r\n                              Absolute playback-speed multiplier; must be finite and positive.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media change-video-speed --input /tmp/in.mp4 --output /tmp/out.mp4 --speed 1.5\r\nNOTES\r\n  Video speed changes preserve audio pitch.\r\n  If encoded output duration drifts by more than 100ms, the output is deleted and the command fails.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Change a whole local video's playback speed and create a new video.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input media file path.\r\n          --output TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Output media file path.\r\n          --speed FLOAT:POSITIVE REQUIRED \r\n                              Absolute playback-speed multiplier; must be finite and positive.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media change-video-speed --input /tmp/in.mp4 --output /tmp/out.mp4 --speed 1.5\r\nNOTES\r\n  Video speed changes preserve audio pitch.\r\n  If encoded output duration drifts by more than 100ms, the output is deleted and the command fails.\r\n",
